      "id": 1,
      "text": "Conewango was carved out of Little Valley in 1823, with its first town meeting held at John Darling’s house.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/town-of-conewango/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "John Darling Road, just northwest of the town hall, honors the first supervisor of Conewango.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/town-of-conewango/",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s inaugural picnic in 1905 drew residents to the square by horse and buggy, a tradition that began with a dish to pass.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellington%2C_New_York",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A saw‑mill on Mill Street, once called Willow Street, served as the town’s industrial heart in the 1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellington%2C_New_York",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Early Conewango relied on several saw‑mills, where most townsfolk worked when not engaged in other trades.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellington%2C_New_York",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The 1865 flood on September 8 turned Twenty‑Eighth Creek into a raging river of logs, devastating homes and the town hall.",
